# Reminder-only beat for demo step 1b: protolens on a clean capture.
#
# This beat never *moves* the view by hand — every step keeps the cursor
# on the root (`node: /`), folds the message down to its top-level fields,
# and unfolds plus highlights the one field it is talking about. So the
# viewport never scrolls between steps: the message stays rooted at the
# top and only one field opens at a time. The presenter still runs the
# interactive gestures (`w`, `v`, `z`, `a`) live. Advance with space or
# Enter.
#
# Invocation (from grehack2026.sh):
#   protolens --descriptor-set life.desc capture/000001-request.pb \
#       --script beats/capture

title: Reading one message with protolens

steps:
  - text: |
      The capture, opened against life.desc.

      protolens renders it as textproto, enriched with annotations
      (press `a` to hide / show them), and it inferred the type:
      StepRequest.

      👋 Reminders — try these by hand:
      - arrow keys / mouse to move
      - `z` or the triangles to fold / unfold a message
      - hover over the root type for its full name and score
    node: /

  - text: |
      A StepRequest has three top-level fields. The first — highlighted —
      is `grid`, a nested Grid message: rows of cells.

      👋 Press space.
    node: /
    fold: ["/ 1", "/1 Z"]
    search: /1

  - text: |
      The second is `rules` — another nested message, with the birth and
      survival ranges and the topology.

      👋 Press space.
    node: /
    fold: ["/ 1", "/2 Z"]
    search: /2

  - text: |
      The third is `generation` — a scalar `uint64`. Drop to wire level
      with `w`: the raw bytes, the tag, the wire type, the varint groups.

      👋 Press `w` on `generation`, then `w` again to close it.
    node: /
    fold: ["/ 1", "/3 Z"]
    search: /3

  - text: |
      On a field whose type is a named message or enum (not a bare
      scalar), press `v`.

      protolens hands off to Neovim, opened at that type's declaration in
      the reconstructed .proto source — the SourceCodeInfo reproto
      synthesized, resolved against the proto/ stub beside life.desc.

      👋 Press `v` on `grid` or `rules`, look at the declaration, come back.
    node: /
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    search: /1

  - text: |
      That is the whole loop: a type recovered from the binary, a message
      read in the clear, the wire underneath one keystroke away — and from
      a byte on the wire to the line of reconstructed source that defines
      it, and back.

      👋 Type `:q` to quit protolens when you are done.
    node: /
